n rallies UAB to 30-17 come-from-behind victory over East Carolina in OT","description":"— Ryder Burton threw a 6-yard touchdown pass to Rod Robinson II in overtime and Delvon Gulley followed with an 80-yard interception return to wrap up UAB’s come-from-behind 30-17 victory over East Carolina on Thursday night.","story":"BIRMINGHAM, Ala. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5057381/ryder-burton\" target=\"_new\">Ryder Burton</a> threw a 6-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4918110/rod-robinson-ii\" target=\"_new\">Rod Robinson II</a> in overtime and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5227913/delvon-gulley\" target=\"_new\">Delvon Gulley</a> followed with an 80-yard interception return to wrap up UAB’s come-from-behind 30-17 victory over East Carolina on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              East Carolina (3-3, 1-1 American Conference) used 14 plays to march 75 yards on the game's opening drive, scoring on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5075800/emory-williams\" target=\"_new\">Emory Williams</a>' 3-yard touchdown toss to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870770/ray-ray-joseph-jr\" target=\"_new\">Ray Ray Joseph Jr</a>. for a 7-0 lead that held through the first quarter.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5159027/dawson-quarterman\" target=\"_new\">Dawson Quarterman</a> recovered a fumble by receiver <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5125012/ismael-smith-flores\" target=\"_new\">Ismael Smith Flores</a> in the end zone after a 16-yard pass from Willliams and the Pirates took a 14-0 lead 47 seconds into the second quarter.\n\n\r\n              UAB (4-3, 2-1) cut it to 14-3 with six minutes left on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5151663/jonah-delange\" target=\"_new\">Jonah Delange</a>'s 41-yard field goal and the score stood at halftime.\n\n\r\n              UAB got a 26-yarder from Delange with 6:44 left in the third quarter and a 50-yarder with 1:26 remaining to get the Blazers within five points heading to the fourth.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5089443/noah-perez\" target=\"_new\">Noah Perez</a> kicked a career-long 43-yard field goal to stretch East Carolina's advantage to 23-15 with 9:24 remaining.\n\n\r\n              Burton drove the Blazers 93 yards in 10 plays without a timeout, connecting with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4897730/bam-mcreynolds\" target=\"_new\">Bam McReynolds</a> for a 17-yard touchdown with 35 seconds left. Burton ran it in for two points to tie it 17-all and force OT.\n\n\r\n              Burton completed 18 of 36 passes for 256 yards. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4711421/cj-smith\" target=\"_new\">CJ Smith</a> had eight receptions for 119 yards.\n\n\r\n              Williams totaled 126 yards on 18-for-27 passing with two touchdowns and the late pick-6. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079419/tj-engleman-jr\" target=\"_new\">TJ Engleman Jr</a>. had 104 yards on 26 carries.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              East Carolina: At Memphis on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              UAB: At South Florida on Oct. 31.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-10-16T03:37:26Z"}}